        "https://www.nbcnews.com/world/iran/iran-says-choice-reopening-hormuz-rests-united-states-offer-rcna599956",
        "https://www.wionews.com/world/will-wait-for-official-us-response-says-araghchi-after-trump-rejects-iran-s-strait-of-hormuz-proposal-1790482861014"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-03"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "headline": "US deploys two additional Patriot batteries to Saudi Arabia and Qatar to protect energy sites",
      "detail": "Axios reported Oct 1-2, citing two US officials and a regional source, that the US deployed two additional Patriot batteries — one to Saudi Arabia to protect a key oil facility and one to Qatar to protect a gas facility — to reassure allies ahead of possible renewed major operations against Iran. US officials said Saudi and Qatari leaders had lobbied Trump in early August against striking Iranian energy infrastructure.",
      "where": "Saudi Arabia and Qatar",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/world/us-sends-additional-patriot-batteries-to-protect-saudi-qatari-energy-sites-report/4075620"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-02"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "headline": "UK renewables offset £5.9bn in gas imports as Hormuz disruption drives gas to 189p/therm",
      "detail": "UK wind and solar generated a record 41% share of UK electricity in 2026 to date vs 25% from gas; gas generation down ~10% year-on-year while wind+solar up 14%. Analysis found wind+solar avoided £5.9 billion in gas imports since February, equivalent to >100 LNG tankers, with £1.3 billion saved in September alone on ~10 TWh output. UK wholesale gas averaged 189p per therm in September, highest since 2022 crisis, vs 90p from 2023-early 2026 and 134p since March, driven by Hormuz disruption and low European stocks. Prediction markets priced prolonged closure at ~2-3% chance of normalization by July/September after July 7 vessel attacks (likely, market snapshot).",
      "where": "United Kingdom; global gas and shipping markets",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-wind-and-solar-save-uk-from-gas-imports-worth-5-9bn-during-hormuz-crisis",
        "https://decrypt.co/364914/prediction-markets-strait-of-hormuz-oil-traders"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-01"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-01",
      "headline": "UK makes new arrest in RAF Fairford plot probe as PM cites strong indications of Iran link; Iran denies",
      "detail": "Five British nationals arrested Sept 28 near RAF Fairford (160 km west of London, used by US B-1/B-52s for Iran strikes since Feb 28) were released on bail by Sept 29-30; police found no explosives but retrieved petrol and continue to investigate whether it was surveillance, dry run or stunt. On Oct 1 UK counter-terror police arrested a 27-year-old dual UK-Iranian national in London on suspicion of preparing terrorist acts linked to the incident. PM Andy Burnham said Oct 1 there were \"strong indications\" Iran played a part, without providing evidence; Iran's embassy Sept 28 and Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi Oct 1 categorically denied any link.",
      "where": "RAF Fairford, United Kingdom",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/1/uk-says-iran-may-be-linked-to-alleged-airbase-plot-drawing-angry-denial",
