    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-28",
      "headline": "Five arrested near US bomber base RAF Fairford; UK PM cites strong indications of Iran link, Iran denies",
      "detail": "Five British nationals aged 23-25 from London were arrested in early hours of Sept 28 near RAF Fairford in Gloucestershire after three white vans were reported heading toward the base; all were released on bail Sept 29. RAF Fairford is US Air Force-operated and has been used for B-1 missions against Iran; IRGC said in July any base used to attack Iran is a legitimate target. A three-day search including bomb disposal found no explosives but retrieved a quantity of petrol (likely, single sourcing); one suspect reportedly called 999 about an hour before a farmer alerted authorities. UK counter-terrorism head Laurence Taylor said a line of inquiry is whether offences were by proxies working for a foreign state; Defence Secretary Wes Streeting declined to speculate.",
      "where": "RAF Fairford, Gloucestershire, UK",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/1/uk-says-iran-may-be-linked-to-alleged-airbase-plot-drawing-angry-denial",
