    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-26",
      "headline": "Trump publicly rejects Iran's seven-day Hormuz reopening offer; mediators still working",
      "detail": "Iran, via Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi at the UN General Assembly and via Qatar, offered to reopen the Strait and resume nuclear talks within seven days if the US released frozen funds, lifted oil sanctions and ended its naval blockade within 4-5 days. Trump publicly rejected outside the White House South Lawn on Sept 26, saying the proposal would not be acceptable because Iran is \"losing so badly.\" As of Sept 28 mediators were still working and the US had not conveyed a formal rejection through channels; three regional officials and a senior US official told AP the public rejection may be a negotiating tactic (likely, single AP sourcing). The Wall Street Journal, citing unnamed US officials (likely, single outlet), reported Trump privately doubts Tehran will meet his demands and expects a renewed bombing campaign after the November midterms.",
      "where": "Washington, D.C. and UN General Assembly, New York",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/26/trump-rejects-irans-seven-day-roadmap-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz",
        "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/26/trump-rejects-irans-conditional-ceasefire-proposal-wsj-reports.html",
        "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/mediators-still-working-on-u-s-iran-deal-after-trump-rejected-latest-tehran-proposal"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-01"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-26",
      "headline": "Saudi-led forces strike Houthi logistics in Marib and near Bab al-Mandeb; Houthis claim 27 Saudi airstrikes",
      "detail": "Saudi and Yemeni government-aligned forces launched drone strikes Sept 26 on a Houthi weapons depot in Jubah District (southern Marib) and a vehicle in al Kasara (northwestern Marib), and operated on high ground at Jabal Naman and Jabal Kahbub near the Bab al-Mandeb. Houthi military spokesperson Yahya Sarea claimed (likely, single source) Saudi Arabia launched 27 airstrikes Sept 26 on bridges and roads in Taiz, Marib, Saada, Amran, Ibb and Hajjah, including damage to al Dalil Bridge in Ibb, to disrupt Houthi ground lines.",
      "where": "Marib, Ibb, Taiz and Bab al-Mandeb area, Yemen",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.criticalthreats.org/analysis/iran-update-special-evening-edition-september-26-2026"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-01"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-25",
      "headline": "Houthis hit Saudi airspace and threaten wider strikes while controlling Bab al-Mandeb approaches",
      "detail": "Saudi air defenses intercepted two Houthi ballistic missiles near Khamis Mushait and two drones near Riyadh on Sept 25-26, with civil defense warnings for Khamis Mushait, Jizan and Abha. Houthi Defense Minister Mohammed al Atifi and Chief of Staff Yusuf al Madani threatened Sept 25 to attack Saudi military bases and strategic/economic targets if red lines are violated. In recent weeks Houthis seized territory along Yemen's Red Sea coast and islands overseeing the Bab al-Mandeb and disabled the 1,200-km Saudi East-West pipeline and disrupted the Jazan export hub that had been used to bypass Hormuz. France announced Sept 24 it will deploy soldiers, radar and air-defense to protect Yanbu, terminus of the pipeline; UK pledged defensive support.",
      "where": "Khamis Mushait, Riyadh, Jizan, Abha, Saudi Arabia; Bab al-Mandeb, Red Sea",
      "verification": "researched",
